  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Growing vegetables in the desert with the OASIS urban greenhouse</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rovero Systems, a Dutch company founded in 1968, specializes in designing and deploying turn-key polyethylene-covered greenhouses for horticulture. Employing 23 people, Rovero stands out in the predominantly glass greenhouse market in the Netherlands by focusing on innovative poly greenhouses. Recently, Rovero has expanded into urban applications, such as rooftop farms and community farms (not on rooftops but on the ground). The OASIS urban greenhouses will be delivered as complete turn-key project, including irrigation and growing systems, ready for immediate use. There is a version for the use on rooftops with storm resistance and there is a version that can be placed in any regular greenhouse location. A key part of this strategy is collaborating with Urban Ponics to launch and expand projects in the Middle East and other regions in the Middle East and Northern Africa (MENA) area. Rovero operates in over 20 countries through an active agent network.With this DHI demonstration project, Rovero and Urban Ponics aim to demonstrate that the OASIS system can thrive in the Egyptian desert climate while providing significant reductions in water use, pesticide dependency and production costs. By demonstrating this production model, potential investors in urban farming, such as professional growers, food suppliers and project developers, will see the benefits of this scalable model.The expected export of greenhouses to the project in three years could quickly reach at least &#x20ac;9 million.</narrative>
  </description>
